Q: AngularJS Get Filtered Scope onClick A: <p>You can assign filteredItems with the following syntax:</p>

<pre><code>{{filteredItem = (portals|myFilter:or| filter:search )}}
&lt;a ng-href='#here' ng-click='go(filteredItem)' &gt;click me&lt;/a&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>You can check the below snippet for an example.</p>

<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="true">
<div class="snippet-code snippet-currently-hidden">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>angular.module("myApp", []).controller("myCtrl", function($scope) {
  $scope.items = ["apple", "banana", "orange"];
})</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;script src="https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/angularjs/1.2.23/angular.min.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;html&gt;

&lt;body ng-app="myApp"&gt;
  &lt;div ng-controller="myCtrl"&gt;
    &lt;input ng-model="query"/&gt;
    {{filteredItems = (items | filter:query)}}
    &lt;div&gt;Filtered Items: {{filteredItems}}&lt;div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;

&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: Defaulted three-way comparison operator with a return type different from the comparison category (C++20) A: <p>minimal fix:</p>
<pre><code>    int operator&lt;=&gt;(const BB&amp; other) const
    {
        return b &lt;=&gt; other.b;
    }
</code></pre>
<p>instead of <code>int operator&lt;=&gt; (const BB &amp;other) const = default;</code></p>
